          "back": {
            "text": "C: Black's knight covers e5, so the trade wins nothing there — with no knight on c6 the same sequence ends 6.Nxe5, a clean pawn (that is the 3...Bg4? line).\n\nWe trade a more active pawn for a passive one and therefore help Black to gain scope for their pieces, in particular the king's bishop, which is limited by the d6-pawn.\n\nBlack has lost castling rights, but this is less of an issue once the queens are traded."
          }
